4173}}] [:step/id #uuid "5b87ea40-1246-51f3-bbc8-ce6933f88cdd" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754180 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754136} :step/id #uuid "5b87ea40-1246-51f3-bbc8-ce6933f88cdd" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754235}}] [:step/id #uuid "62d9e667-c6f9-53b6-9881-a8e528484aae" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754184 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754155} :step/id #uuid "62d9e667-c6f9-53b6-9881-a8e528484aae" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754248}}] [:step/id #uuid "6a63bcf9-9957-5a72-967f-aed310edc2c0" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754186 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754238} :step/id #uuid "6a63bcf9-9957-5a72-967f-aed310edc2c0" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754180}}] [:step/id #uuid "77280565-db93-548d-9792-8f3b0c73d61f" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754191 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754138} :step/id #uuid "77280565-db93-548d-9792-8f3b0c73d61f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754145}}] [:step/id #uuid "7daf21f1-eeea-50dd-8d33-29a8329c72b4" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754193 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754254} :step/id #uuid "7daf21f1-eeea-50dd-8d33-29a8329c72b4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754240}}] [:tutorial/id #uuid "3291e1c0-7251-50f2-bea9-669366fc030c" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754155 :tutorial/content "**MTH 255 — Final Exam Study Guide**\n\nDue: unknown\nExam schedule from source: Week 11 according to the Final Exam Schedule, in the usual classroom. Exact calendar date and time are not specified in this PDF.\nDate imported: 2026-11-06\nSource: [255 Final Exam Guide_v1.pdf](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FSG-2%2F255%20Final%20Exam%20Guide_v1.pdf)\nStudy format: These 40 study objectives do not require submitted answers. Study links are added navigation; component-only matches and remaining coverage gaps are labeled below.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### Exam information\n\n- **When:** Week 11 according to the Final Exam Schedule.\n- **Where:** Our usual classroom.\n- **Duration:** 110 minutes.\n- **Resources:** You are not allowed to use any resource (calculator, notes, etc.) for the exam. Bring a pencil and an eraser.\n- **Sections covered:** 5.7 and 6.1–6.8.\n\n### Question formats\n\nThe exam will have two classes of problems:\n\n- Multiple-choice, choose many, true/false, fill-in-the-blank, and matching problems. For most of these problems you do not receive partial credit.\n- Show-your-work problems. These are similar to the ones appearing on written homework in terms of appearance and difficulty. You receive partial credit for partial progress toward the answer on these problems.\n\n### Preparation advice\n\n- Look back to what you’ve done in class:\n  - Review problems in Achieve.\n  - Revisit the written homework problems (and keys).\n  - Revisit the recitation worksheets (and keys).\n- Look at the exercises at the end of each section in the textbook.\n- Look at the review exercises at the end of each chapter in the textbook.\n\n### Topic list\n\nThe source states: **This is NOT a comprehensive list of topics appearing on the exam.**\n\n| Source section | Study objectives |\n| --- | --- |\n| Section 6.1: Vector Fields | 1–6 |\n| Section 6.2: Line Integrals | 7–10 |\n| Section 6.3: Conservative Vector Fields | 11–14 |\n| Section 6.4: Green’s Theorem | 15–21 |\n| Section 6.5: Divergence and Curl | 22–25 |\n| Section 5.7: Change of Variables in Multiple Integrals | 26–29 |\n| Section 6.6: Surface Integrals | 30–34 |\n| Section 6.7: Stokes’ Theorem | 35–37 |\n| Section 6.8: The Divergence Theorem | 38–40 |" :tutorial/id #uuid "3291e1c0-7251-50f2-bea9-669366fc030c" :tutorial/title "Exam information and preparation advice"}] [:question/id #uuid "895c6fe8-0b08-5fc1-9f3d-01ed2d7aca52" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754198 :question/id #uuid "895c6fe8-0b08-5fc1-9f3d-01ed2d7aca52" :question/problem "Source study objective: (24), PDF page 2. Section 6.5: Divergence and Curl.\n\nUse the curl test to determine if a 3D vector field is conservative."}] [:question/id #uuid "8ef745fb-f653-50c5-a91d-058bce0ba35e" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754200 :question/id #uuid "8ef745fb-f653-50c5-a91d-058bce0ba35e" :question/problem "Source study objective: (27), PDF page 3. Section 5.7: Change of Variables in Multiple Integrals.\n\nUnderstand how a transformation maps regions to regions\n\n- a region in the $uv$-plane to a region in the $xy$-plane\n- a solid region in the $uvw$-space to a solid region in the $xyz$-space"}] [:question/id #uuid "9a49aaa4-d2f2-5857-9117-3cf681182e99" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754207 :question/id #uuid "9a49aaa4-d2f2-5857-9117-3cf681182e99" :question/problem "Source study objective: (17), PDF page 2. Section 6.4: Green’s Theorem.\n\nDistinguish between the circulation form and the flux form of Green’s Theorem."}] [:question/id #uuid "9b9492e1-c6b7-5c28-8b2f-74a417a8683d" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754208 :question/id #uuid "9b9492e1-c6b7-5c28-8b2f-74a417a8683d" :question/problem "Source study objective: (1), PDF page 2. Section 6.1: Vector Fields.\n\nSketch or identify a vector field given its algebraic formula."}] [:question/id #uuid "a4725d87-4144-5055-99c0-b31caa383f0c" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754211 :question/id #uuid "a4725d87-4144-5055-99c0-b31caa383f0c" :question/problem "Source study objective: (4), PDF page 2. Section 6.1: Vector Fields.\n\nFor a conservative field, know what an equipotential curve is."}] [:question/id #uuid "a6f1fd49-be0e-5496-a7e4-710e5e8a56bc" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754212 :question/id #uuid "a6f1fd49-be0e-5496-a7e4-710e5e8a56bc" :question/problem "Source study objective: (15), PDF page 2. Section 6.4: Green’s Theorem.\n\nApply Green’s Theorem to evaluate line integrals along closed, positively oriented curves in the plane."}] [:question/id #uuid "a78c1e98-e784-5400-9870-6e1c90c38b49" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754214 :question/id #uuid "a78c1e98-e784-5400-9870-6e1c90c38b49" :question/problem "Source study objective: (2), PDF page 2. Section 6.1: Vector Fields.\n\nUnderstand and identify conservative vector fields."}] [:question/id #uuid "b72adf84-2be0-5b84-b1ab-613268794b0d" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754217 :question/id #uuid "b72adf84-2be0-5b84-b1ab-613268794b0d" :question/problem "Source study objective: (34), PDF page 3. Section 6.6: Surface Integrals.\n\nUnderstand how unit normal vectors and surface orientation are connected."}] [:question/id #uuid "bea61dd4-6908-561a-b202-a8e02f4dc246" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754219 :question/id #uuid "bea61dd4-6908-561a-b202-a8e02f4dc246" :question/problem "Source study objective: (13), PDF page 2. Section 6.3: Conservative Vector Fields.\n\nFind a potential function for a given conservative vector field."}] [:question/id #uuid "c0a70b0a-adf8-592d-ae72-de2716bb90f0" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754220 :question/id #uuid "c0a70b0a-adf8-592d-ae72-de2716bb90f0" :question/problem "Source study objective: (25), PDF page 2. Section 6.5: Divergence and Curl.\n\nKnow the important identities involving the gradient, the divergence, and the curl:\n\n- the curl of the gradient is zero.\n- the divergence of the curl is zero."}] [:question/id #uuid "c2c75d68-6784-5c67-8e7b-6ef7f1d74f6b" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754221 :question/id #uuid "c2c75d68-6784-5c67-8e7b-6ef7f1d74f6b" :question/problem "Source study objective: (20), PDF page 2. Section 6.4: Green’s Theorem.\n\nFind a stream function for a given source-free vector field."}] [:question/id #uuid "c37341e5-4993-5fc9-b5d1-97af5f0e0da9" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754222 :question/id #uuid "c37341e5-4993-5fc9-b5d1-97af5f0e0da9" :question/problem "Source study objective: (40), PDF page 3. Section 6.8: The Divergence Theorem.\n\nUnderstand important physical applications like Gauss’s Law."}] [:question/id #uuid "c5dce64c-aaa3-5863-934d-927d915456ec" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186754224 :question/id #uuid "c5dce64c-aaa3-5863-934d-927d915456ec" :question/problem "Source study objective: (8), PDF page 2. Section 6.2: Line Integrals.\n\nCalculate the